Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day. By 4 October the desk
had **412 unique reports** merged into #4471.

**Merged as one issue, but it contains two causes.** Both affect tenants whose locale writes the
day before the month. The shared parser reads every date month first. Separately, `booking-v3`
shows a `MM/DD/YYYY` hint to those tenants, so their input is interpreted using the wrong order.

<Callout>
Known. Split the work into the parser fix and the booking-v3 hint fix.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Problems to file

### Parser reads day-first dates as month-first

**379 reports** belong to this cause. The shared parser reads dates month first even for day-first
locales, flipping the day and month in the resulting booking.

### booking-v3 shows the wrong date hint

**33 reports** belong to this cause. The `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` for day-first
locales, directing people to enter dates in an order the tenant's locale does not use.

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Lessons

- A large ticket can contain more than one cause. Group reports by tenant behavior, not only by intake tag.
- Keep each cause in its own ticket so engineering can count and fix it independently.
- Preserve the computed report counts in the component-backed table.

